  "problem": "The growth rate of the rabbit population $P(t)$ in a wildlife preserve is jointly proportional to the rabbit population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the preserve’s carrying capacity and the rabbit population.\n\nGiven that the constant of proportionality is $0.0025$ and the carrying capacity is $1200,$ find an expression for the rabbit population after $t$ years, given that there were $200$ rabbits in the preserve initially.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"right\">\n      $P(t)\\,=\\,\\,$\n    </td>\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      $1200$\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      $1\\,+\\,$ {{field-1}}\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table>",
